

**Figure 9.5**: _Zeros of \(Y_{n}(z)\) and \(Y^{\prime}_{n}(z)\)._

**Figure 9.5** shows the approximate distribution of the complex zeros of \(Y_{n}(z)\) in the region [arg \(z|\!\leq\!\pi\). The figure is symmetrical about the real axis. The two curves on the left extend to infinity, having the asymptotes

\[{\mathscr{I}}\!z\!=\!\pm\frac{1}{2}\ln\,3\!=\!+.54931\quad.\quad.\]

There are an infinite number of zeros near each of these curves.

The two curves extending from \(z\!=\!-n\) to \(z\!=\!n\) and bounding an eye-shaped domain intersect the imaginary axis at the points \(\pm i(na\!+\!b)\), where

\[a\!=\!\sqrt{t_{0}^{2}\!-\!1}\!=\!.66274\quad.\quad.\]

\[b\!=\!\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{1\!-\!t_{0}^{2}}\ln\,2\!=\!.19146\quad.\quad.\]

